able is included,” “confirm the listed length is 120 cm,” or “cancel if only blue is available.”\n\nFor compatibility risks, request confirmation before purchase. QC images can show appearance, labels, and visible condition, but may not prove fit, electronic function, material composition, or authenticity. Resolve listing questions before the seller ships and use the warehouse stage for evidence that can genuinely be seen or measured."
      ],
      [
        "Read order status as a decision clock",
        "Sugargoo’s official cancellation guide lists stages including Pending Payment, Payment in Progress, Purchasing, Shipped, and Completed. These labels indicate which corrections may still be practical.\n\nPending Payment is the easiest stage to edit or abandon. Payment in Progress means confirmation is underway, so avoid creating duplicates. Purchasing means the agent is buying or coordinating with the seller. If you spot an error, contact support immediately, but cancellation is not guaranteed because the seller may already have accepted the order.\n\nShipped means the seller has sent the item toward the warehouse. A change now usually becomes a return or exchange request. Completed means the product has entered the warehouse process, where the order record and QC evidence guide the keep, exchange, or return decision.\n\nReview new orders after payment confirmation and again when they enter Purchasing. Look for price adjustments, seller questions, missing information, or unusual delays. Escalate when a decision is needed, not merely because a status has remained unchanged for a few hours."
      ],
      [
        "Create intervention thresholds before you pay",
        "Do not wait for a problem to decide what counts as a problem. Set simple intervention thresholds before payment. Examples include the highest acceptable item price, maximum domestic shipping charge, latest useful dispatch date, whether partial quantity is acceptable, and which substitutions are forbidden.\n\nThese thresholds make seller questions faster to answer and reduce impulse decisions. They are especially useful for limited-stock products, pre-orders, customized goods, and wholesale listings where the final amount may differ from the headline price. A threshold is not a promise that the seller will comply; it is your instruction to the purchasing agent about when to continue and when to stop.\n\nAlso decide when silence becomes actionable. A short unchanged status is not automatically a 